-- CA_0141_seed_la_june_runoffs_compton_pomona.sql
-- Seed the three LA-County CITY seats that went to a Nov 3 2026 runoff and are not yet on the
-- November ballot, and give the two cities' council districts real geometry so each runoff
-- reaches ONLY its own district's voters.
--
-- WHICH SEATS. California city offices elected in a June "primary nominating" election are
-- decided outright by a June majority; otherwise the top two meet in November. From the LA
-- County Registrar-Recorder's final June 2 2026 canvass (results.lavote.gov/text-results/4338,
-- "Results as of 06/26/2026"), checked against every June city contest in the county:
--   Compton Mayor              Sharif 41.70%, Spicer 18.43%   -> RUNOFF   SEED
--   Compton Council District 2 Tinson 30.44%, Perry 23.14%    -> RUNOFF   SEED (open: Spicer, the
--                                                                 holder, is in the Mayor runoff)
--   Compton Council District 3 Bowers 51.19%                  -> won outright (skip)
--   Compton City Clerk / City Treasurer                       -> won outright (skip)
--   Pomona Council District 2  Preciado 45.38%, Elizalde 33.03% -> RUNOFF SEED
--   Pomona Council Districts 3 and 5                          -> won outright (skip)
--   Long Beach, Los Angeles, Pasadena, Glendale, LAUSD, LBUSD -> every seat decided in June
--     (LA City runoffs were CA_0137). All other June cities are general-law (plurality, no runoff).
-- Cross-checked: the Pomona D2 and Compton Mayor runoffs are reported by the city and local press
-- (The Pomonan, 2026-09-01; LA Wave, June 2026).
--
-- WHY GEOMETRY. Compton's four council districts had their own geo_ids
-- ('compton-council-district-N') but NO polygon, so no address reached the four sitting council
-- members at all. Pomona's six council districts all pointed at the whole-city polygon
-- (geo_id '0658072'), so every Pomona address returned all six members -- and a District 2 race
-- bound there would show citywide. This migration loads one polygon per district and points each
-- district row at it (mtfcc 'X0001', the local council-district layer the Part A join and
-- MTFCC_DISTRICT_TYPE_GUARD already admit for LOCAL).
--
-- GEOMETRY SOURCE. The LA County Registrar-Recorder's own precinct file -- the layer the county
-- uses to assign every ballot -- which tags each precinct with its city and council district
-- (DST_CITY / DIV_CITY):
--   https://public.gis.lacounty.gov/public/rest/services/LACounty_Dynamic/Political_Boundaries/MapServer/34
-- Read 2026-09-22 (33,236 precincts). Each district = the union of its precincts (Compton 'CO'
-- divisions 1-4, Pomona 'PY' divisions 1-6); seam slivers under 100 m2 dropped, simplified at
-- 2e-6 deg (~0.2 m). CURRENCY CHECK: the same dissolve for Monterey Park ('MP') matches the city's
-- own 2026 redistricting map already in the DB (CC_0023) at IoU 0.994-0.995, so the precinct file
-- carries 2026-vintage council lines. Compton District 4 keeps one real 0.5 km2 hole (an
-- unincorporated county island).
--
-- RACES go on '2026 LA County General' (d91a20ce-557e-4615-a31b-5b2b3df2ed14), where the app already groups LA-County city
-- races (Mayor of Los Angeles, CA_0137). Nonpartisan -> primary_party NULL; party never stored.
-- Each race reuses the existing seated office, so no new office needs a holder.
-- Candidates: Sharif, Spicer and Preciado already have politician rows and are linked; Tinson,
-- Perry and Elizalde have none (only campaign-committee stubs) and stay unlinked, as their June
-- primary rows were. Incumbent = the sitting holder of THAT seat: Sharif (Mayor), Preciado (D2).
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: geofences on (geo_id, mtfcc); district repoints guarded on the old value; races on
-- (election_id, position_name); candidates on (race_id, lower(full_name)).

BEGIN;

-- ─── 1. Council-district polygons (4 Compton + 6 Pomona) ────────────────────────────────
